WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.620
There are a lot more publishers of comic books
than just the big dogs of Marvel and DC.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:11.440
Let's not forget about Valiant Comics, originators
of badass heroes with silly names like Manowar,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.560
Ninjak, the Eternal Warrior, and Bloodshot.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.240
While Marvel and DC have done a very good
job of launching their properties from the

00:00:19.249 --> 00:00:23.630
page to the big screen, Hollywood has been
slow to grant a Valiant character their own

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.420
feature film.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.180
That's all about to change, because a Bloodshot
movie is on the way.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:34.140
Created by Kevin VanHook, Don Perlin, and
Bob Layton in 1992, Bloodshot a seemingly

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:39.500
un-killable and invincible scientifically
restructured super-trooper has sold more than

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.440
seven million comics since his debut.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.200
There's clearly an audience for a Bloodshot
movie, and Sony has finally decided to make

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:46.780
it happen.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.080
Here's everything you need to know about the
film, which is sure to be action-packed, over

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.320
the top, and drenched in buckets of blood.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.100
C'mon… it's in the name!

00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:01.380
Years ago, the only time filmgoers got a chance
to see big, expensive, dazzling, and action-packed

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:04.059
movies at the cineplex was the summer.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:08.900
The hottest months of the year were reserved
for summer blockbusters, huge and extravagant

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:12.420
feasts for the senses starring Hollywood's
most popular actors.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.330
Appetites for these movies proved so high
that studios started releasing them well before

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.440
summer, and now in the dead of winter.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.260
Two of the most recent and biggest-ever comic
book-based films hit movie theaters in mid-February:

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.600
Deadpool and Black Panther.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:32.260
Huh… it's almost like Marvel has cornered
the comic book movie market, and its competitors

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.820
should just give up or something…

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:38.840
"Are you done?

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.400
Are… are you, are you, are you done?"

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:45.480
Kidding, kidding… sort of.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:50.660
Anyway, movie fans need some alternatives
to the other stuff that dominates movie theaters

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:55.310
in the early months of the year, and 2020
will continue this trend.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:02:00.640
Bloodshot was initially scheduled to be released
over the weekend of February 21, 2020.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.600
Sony confirmed the date with the film's first
trailer, which hit the internet in October

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.180
2019.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.000
In December, however, the studio announced
that Bloodshot had been pushed back just a

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.140
few weeks, to March 13th.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:19.000
Obviously, one-man action squad Vin Diesel
is the biggest name attached to the upcoming

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:24.920
film adaptation of the Bloodshot comics, heading
up the cast as Ray Garrison, deceased Marine

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:28.060
turned reborn overpowered soldier supreme.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:28.920
How?

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.500
Nano-machines, son!

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:31.420
That's how!

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.680
"Nano-machines, son!"

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:42.260
Guy Pearce, best known for his role in memory-oriented
thriller Memento is playing Dr. Emil Harting,

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.280
a "think-outside-the-box" mad scientist leading
the experiments on Garrison.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:52.700
Sam Heughan, the breakout star of Starz time-travel/period
piece Outlander, is said to be playing Jimmy

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.660
Dalton, a Navy SEAL and super-soldier in his
own right.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:01.520
Eiza Gonzalez perhaps best known for playing
Darling in Baby Driver stars as the mysterious

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.790
Ms. KT, a member of the inner circle of a
strange underground organization.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.930
She's joined by longtime New Girl star Lamorne
Morris, who fills the comic relief role of

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:12.920
Wilfred Wigans.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.660
"That is absolutely fantastic."

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:20.300
Judging by the first trailer, there looks
to be a lot going on in the film version of

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.800
Bloodshot.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:25.500
Vin Diesel is introduced as a humble Marine
named Ray, and all seems to be going well

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.800
as he reunites with his beloved wife Gina
in a lovely seaside town... only to wake up

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:35.100
in a cold and dark research facility connected
to a bunch of machines, Matrix-style.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:41.700
Ray learns from resident scientist Dr. Emil
Harting that he actually died as did Gina

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:47.010
but he's now under the watchful eye of RST,
a corporation that "rebuilds" U.S. military

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:47.580
assets.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.580
A shadowy corporation with access to cutting-edge
science trying to create super soldiers, huh?

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.940
We're sure they won't have any, you know,
ulterior motives or anything.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:00.520
"They've been manipulating you."

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.720
Oh, uh… yeah… scratch that.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.110
Turns out that Ray is the first successful
result of an ongoing program to remake and

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:11.000
enhance soldiers into living weapons.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:16.000
Harting and his associates have injected into
Ray's blood some out-there technology that

00:04:16.019 --> 00:04:21.680
makes him virtually indestructible extra-strong
and able to heal from basically any injury

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.520
within seconds.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.820
With these powers in mind, Ray sets out to
take care of "unfinished business" and get

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.040
vengeance on the men who killed his wife.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.860
To make a long story short: Bloodshot is a
lot like Deadpool …

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.440
"You know, it has always been a dream of mine
to see my face reflected in your helmet as

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.480
you charge at me with murderous intent."

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.780
… only super, suuuper serious and without
any breaking through the fourth wall.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:51.460
There's also an added psychological complication,
as RST just might be manipulating Ray into

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:57.340
pursuing its interests, not his own in other
words, his memories may not be what he thinks

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.120
they are.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.560
Behind the scenes, Bloodshot boasts a creative
team with a wealth of entertainment experience.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:08.340
Studios generally don't hand the reins of
a big-budget extravaganza to brand-new directors,

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.940
but that's exactly what's happening with Dave
Wilson.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:17.060
It's his first feature-length project, building
upon an episode of the sci-fi anthology Love,

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:22.669
Death &amp; Robots and a long career directing
trailers for major video game releases, including

00:05:22.669 --> 00:05:27.560
The Elder Scrolls Online, Mass Effect 2, and
Star Wars: The Old Republic Knights of the

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.620
Fallen Empire.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:33.320
Bloodshot's credits list two screenwriters:
Jeff Wadlow and Eric Heisserer.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.040
Wadlow wrote a couple of episodes of Bates
Motel before penning the scripts for comics

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:43.080
adaptation Kick-Ass 2, the spy farce True
Memoirs of an International Assassin, and

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.880
the scary Truth or Dare.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:49.960
Heisserer got his start in horror, writing
the A Nightmare on Elm Street remake before

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.140
working on the scripts for innovative sci-fi
hits like Arrival and Bird Box.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.100
In today's movie world, it's all about comic
books, superheroes, and cinematic universes.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.680
Disney has its Marvel Cinematic Universe and
Warner Bros. has DC.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.320
Now Sony may be in the early stages of getting
a Valiant-based world of interconnected characters

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:15.080
off the ground, using Bloodshot as its Iron
Man-esque first chapter.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:21.460
According to a Hollywood Reporter news item
from 2015, Sony had plans to make five Valiant

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:27.280
adaptations: two Bloodshot movies, plus two
based on Harbinger, a comic about a superhero

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.280
collective on the lam from a shady organization.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:35.330
After that, the properties would receive their
own Justice League or Avengers-style capper

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.860
with a crossover called Harbinger Wars.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:43.460
Additionally, in 2018, Sony hired American
Gods adaptation writer Maria Melnik for a

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:49.110
screenplay about the slightly meta Valiant
character Faith Herbert, a.k.a. Zephyr, a

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:53.120
comics aficionado who becomes a hero herself
when her telekinetic powers surface.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.060
It's hard to say if this plan is still in
the cards, and a lot rests on Bloodshot being

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.000
a success.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:04.260
Harbinger moved from Sony to Paramount in
September 2019, which could delay the development

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.160
of this particular cinematic universe.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:10.180
Only time and Bloodshot's box office results
will tell.

